    "answer": {
      "short": "$9$.\n\nRationalise each term; all intermediate roots cancel.",
      "worked": "For $n=1,\\ldots,99$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\sqrt n+\\sqrt{n+1}}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{n+1}-\\sqrt n}{(n+1)-n}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt n+\\sqrt{n+1}}&=\\sqrt{n+1}-\\sqrt n.\\end{align*}$$\nWriting the sum as $S$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=(\\sqrt2-1)+(\\sqrt3-\\sqrt2)+\\cdots+(\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt{99})\\\\S&=\\sqrt{100}-1\\\\S&=9.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
